    why_schema: `Schema.org is an invisible data block in the page code (usually JSON-LD). It tells search engines and AI systems explicitly what the page is: an article with author and date, an FAQ with questions and answers, a product. Without it, they have to guess from the layout. We expect at least two different types, plus the type that fits the content: Article on articles, FAQPage on pages with at least three FAQ questions.`,
    fix_schema: `The web agency adds a JSON-LD block to the page template; on articles of type Article with headline, author and date (copy-paste template in the recommendations). It is set up once and then applies to every page of that kind. The editorial team only needs to keep headline, author and date filled in in the CMS.`,
