    why_entities: `AI systems map content to known “entities”: clearly identified organisations, people and topics. When the structured data says who publishes the page, who wrote it and what it is about, and backs this up with a logo or profile links (e.g. Wikipedia, LinkedIn), a system can attribute the statements to the right source. We count six signals: publisher, publisher verifiable, author, author verifiable, linked blocks and topic.`,
    fix_entities: `The web agency adds the details listed above as missing to the template, e.g. the publisher with logo and sameAs links to official profiles, the author with a link to their profile page, @id links between the blocks and the topic via about (template in the recommendations). The editorial team can supply the profile links and topics.`,

