    ev_robotsTxt_blocked_count: `{blocked} of {total} checked crawlers are blocked for this page ({path}).`,
    ev_robotsTxt_blocked_index: `Blocked search engine crawlers: {bots}. Their index is what Google AI Overviews and AI Mode, Microsoft Copilot and partly ChatGPT Search answer from. While blocked, the page drops out of search results and out of these AI answers.`,
    ev_robotsTxt_blocked_search: `Blocked search crawlers: {bots}. They fetch pages for answers in ChatGPT, Claude and Perplexity. While blocked, the page does not appear there as a source.`,
    ev_robotsTxt_blocked_user: `Blocked on-request fetchers: {bots}. These bots open a page when someone asks about it in a chat or pastes the link.`,
    ev_robotsTxt_blocked_training: `Blocked training crawlers: {bots}. This keeps the content out of the training of future language models, but does not stop the page from appearing in AI answers.`,
    why_robotsTxt: `robots.txt is a text file in the root of the website that tells crawlers what they may read. AI providers run different crawlers: training crawlers (e.g. GPTBot, ClaudeBot, CCBot) collect text for future models, while search crawlers (OAI-SearchBot, Claude-SearchBot, PerplexityBot) and on-request fetchers (ChatGPT-User, Claude-User) fetch pages for current answers. Blocking search or on-request bots removes the site from AI answers; blocking only training crawlers does not. The check weighs search crawlers three times and on-request fetchers twice as much as training crawlers. Blocking only training crawlers costs a few points but still passes. Googlebot and Bingbot are checked too: Google’s AI answers and Copilot draw on their search index, so they weigh like search crawlers.`,
    fix_robotsTxt: `Whoever maintains robots.txt (usually the web agency) removes the Disallow rules for the listed search and on-request bots (template in the recommendations). If you do not want AI training, you can keep the training crawlers blocked and only allow the search bots. Also check whether a firewall or CDN (e.g. Cloudflare) blocks the bots as well.`,
    fix_robotsTxt_training: `Only training crawlers are blocked. This is often a deliberate decision and has little effect on visibility in AI answers. If you want to allow training, the web agency removes the Disallow rules for these bots (template in the recommendations); otherwise you can accept the deduction knowingly.`,

